@JayzTwoCents The 5700XT got a silicon respin, black screens weren't a driver issue. 

According to AMD, SAM uses the pdep32 CPU instruction which is emulated via microcode on anything older than Zen 3. I think that implementing SAM without that instruction would still be possible and share your opinion that AMD pulled an anti-consumer move on us. 

Further, AMD's IPC is actually higher as the cards deliver comparable performance with fewer stream processors than Nvidia. Ampere is all about the former INT32 units being able to do FP32 aswell.

